\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0   Sin shall have its due recompense,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 The reward of sin is death:
\par If the Saviour Christ never died,
\par We would not avert justice;
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Jesus has borne all our troubles;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And has borne our deaths as His;
\par 'Twas the blood of Jesus
\par God took as a ransome for our sins
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  God by His death demonstrates that
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 His righteousness swallows death;
\par And that by His act of mercy
\par And death gives us salvation.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  All the pow'r belongs unto Him
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 To forgive believer's sins.
\par So that They have rest in His love
\par And as well, eternal love
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  In this way the holiness of
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 God shall exceed all our sin;
\par His uprightness consumes our sins,
\par And His life consumes our death.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par    6. As at first sin reigned over and
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Dominated us to death,
\par I shall uprightness dominate
\par And lead us back into life
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. And now we no longer serve sin;
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 No more are we transgressors;
\par Jesus reigns supreme in our hearts,
\par And changes our ways as well.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Do we expect from Jesus' blood
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  To become so freed from sin
\par  That no act of vindictiveness
\par Shall be meted to our foes
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9. Never ! I' m dead to transgression;
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 I'm alive with Jesus Christ.
\par Christ by his death has redeemed me,
\par  And for Him I am alive.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  10. And therefore I am not myself
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 It is Christ that lives in me;
\par And I live unto Him only
\par \pard     In His love and in His faith.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

